  "reason": "The best result so far is config_004 (acc=0.5988) using pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, transformer aggregation, and concat fusion. The resnet50 comparison (config_007 concat vs config_010 weighted) showed concat edges out weighted on accuracy (0.579 vs 0.573) but weighted was better on F1 (0.573 vs 0.563), so the fusion choice is genuinely uncertain. Config_005 tests the same strong backbone (pca_n2000 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer) with weighted fusion, directly clarifying whether weighted fusion can match or exceed the 0.599 accuracy with the better image encoder. This is the highest-value exploitation step: it refines the single most promising direction with minimal additional cost (~4.8 GPU hours, comparable to config_004 since only the fusion head changes). With 6 experiments remaining, locking down the optimal fusion before exploring alternative RNA encoders (scgpt, scvi) or aggregation strategies (avgpool) ensures subsequent experiments build on the strongest known base."
}

